---
description: Rule-based weighted scoring engine conventions — use when implementing, modifying, or debugging category or course scoring logic
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

Scoring uses two levels: CategoryScore(C) = sum of points from Interests +
Skills + Academic Performance answers, then MatchPercentage(C) =
(CategoryScore(C) / MaxPossibleScore(C)) x 100. Course-level ranking starts
all 4 courses in a category at the category's Match %, then applies
tie-breaker adjustments (+5% each, max 1-2 per course).

The engine MUST recompute the full score fresh on every submission — never
incrementally add points per section, to avoid double-counting edited
answers. Full weight table and formulas: instructions.md Section 6, and
"6 - 4.4 Complete RuleWeight_Scoring Table + Formula.docx."